data check_reachable_only_from_an_entry_point_the_context_never_calls: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "check_reachable_only_from_an_entry_point_the_context_never_calls" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a check that is real at one entry point is unreachable from the context that holds its subject, and a green there is silence, not a pass** (INVALID STATE: a blocking diagnostic exists, fires under `gunbc compile` / the parse sweep / an enrolled census over a virtual source, and the required fold that actually holds the live subject never calls that pass. The invalid program is writable in the tree the lanes accept. HARM: source review, not any mechanism, is the detector; every later author of the same shape inherits a wall that is cited from the enrolled probe and is not on the path that would have refused them. DISTINGUISHING FACT: a lane that does not run the pass is silent, and silence looks identical to a pass -- that is the class. The named silent hole of a DIFFERENT class, a type-variable scrutinee, is not this: here the checker names the missing constructor when it is asked.)",
    "FIRST SPECIMEN, DESIGN section 4c source-annotation attachment. Trailing, body, and unattached `//` forms refuse at `gunbc compile` and at the required-ci parse sweep (`v1_src_dag_parse` / `run_dag_parse_sweep`). `claim_batch --entry` resolves the annotation-erased projection and never runs that sweep, so a grain or attachment defect in a touched module is invisible to a local loop that is claim_batch alone while every witness reports PASS. The check is not missing; the entry point the author actually runs is.",
    "SECOND SPECIMEN, gunbc#11194 head d75c000465d7ec26bc4b86fd28f212c7a776193d. `gunbc.product.fabric.provider_admission` `ProviderUseRefusal` had thirteen arms. `test.claim.fabric.common_paper_csa_agreement_witness` `accepted_of` matched ten, no catch-all, omitting `PostureJurisdictionsUnread`, `TransferOrLocationUnresolved`, `ProviderAccessPathUnsupported`. The head was green on required-witnesses-build, required-witnesses-floor, heal-generated-artifacts, and witnesses. Found by source review of the arms. THE DISCRIMINATING EXECUTION, same compiler, a two-module fixture of the same shape (imported closed coproduct, concrete parameter, field-binding arms, omit one constructor, no wildcard): `gunbc compile --entry` refused at emit with `NonExhaustiveMatch` `missing variant(s) C` on `match c {`. The exhaustive control compiled with zero diagnostics. Pass: `v1.compiler.infer` match inference -> `check_match_exhaustiveness` on `ConstructorsClosed`. So the concrete-scrutinee wall HOLDS. What did not run it was the required fold.",
    "WHY THE REQUIRED LANES DID NOT SEE IT. `claim_executor --required-ci` is parse, namespace-wave-admission, generated-artifact, regen-fixed-point, floor. Parse does not infer. Floor prepares `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_prefixes` plus changed-witness identities. `test.claim.fabric.common_paper_csa_agreement_witness` matches no prefix. `test.claim.match_exhaustiveness_coproduct_witness` does, and so the checker is exercised every floor over VIRTUAL census sources, not over this live file. Changed-witness identities are only `edited_test_fns`. `FloorDiffEdits.touched_entry_files` is the filtered set of non-data, non-test-fn declaration edits -- the comment on the struct already says that set means run that entry's roster -- and `changed_and_enrolled_witness_identities_with_index` never consumed it. d75c000's hunk in the specimen file deleted a `data` row and a field in `fn posture`, not a `test fn`, so no witness was planned, the module was never strictly resolved, and NonExhaustiveMatch never ran. Type growth on `ProviderUseRefusal` alone would not have planned the consumer either.",
    "NEIGHBOUR, so the two are not conflated. `witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red` owns a claim file that cannot compile and is therefore absent from the execution roster. This class is the CHECK that would have made it fail to compile, sitting on an entry point the required context never calls. The repairs are not substitutes: compiling every claim-root file discharges the neighbour's trigger; wiring the dead `touched_entry_files` set into the prepared subject's seeds discharges THIS specimen's invocation hole for a helper-fn edit in the same file, and does not by itself compile every importer of a grown coproduct. THAT residual is the neighbour's widened trigger (compile every construction site of a type whose declared field or variant set changed), not a second exhaustiveness algorithm.",
    "RUNG found at 1, mitigatable: the checker is real and blocking when invoked; required CI did not invoke it on the live subject. CEILING 2, mechanically preventable: a required path that strictly resolves every module whose non-test, non-data declaration the diff touched (`touched_entry_files` consumed as prepare seeds) makes this specimen refuse. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, capability not artifact: the required floor's prepared subject MUST include the authored module of every path in `touched_entry_files` and refuse a Strict-resolve hard diagnostic, including `NonExhaustiveMatch`. Sufficient for a helper-fn or type-decl edit in the file that carries the non-exhaustive match. Not sufficient, and not claimed as sufficient, for a type-roster change whose only stale match lives in an untouched importer -- that remains the neighbour row's compile-every-construction-site trigger.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
